Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 12:42:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/54] sampler: backend-sampling + MTP safety fixes
 (F2/F1/F3/F4)

F2 - ngram-bias transactional state: clone/copy preserve recent + in_thinking,
backend_init refuses multi-output offload (single shared history).
F1 - constrained full-vocab fallback: with backend candidates filtered by the
prefix, rebuild from raw logits and run the whole chain on the CPU.
F3 - backend_reject hook: grammar/budget rejection resample draws a fresh
uniform instead of reusing the pending backend draw; accept() no double-advance.
F4 - server: skip the probabilistic verifier (forbidden grammar_first+backend)
when a grammar is attached; MTP (no dists) unaffected.

Red/Green: regression test (model-free, real libllama) went 5 FAIL -> 8 PASS.
Reviewed in bench_qwen38/mtp_deep_20260908/reviews/sampling-mtp.md (F5 deferred).
---
 common/sampling.cpp             | 44 ++++++++++++++++++
 include/llama.h                 | 11 +++++
 src/llama-sampler.cpp           | 80 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 tools/server/server-context.cpp |  7 ++-
 4 files changed, 137 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/sampling.cpp b/common/sampling.cpp
index f78879e182e..a3ad633a86a 100644
--- a/common/sampling.cpp
+++ b/common/sampling.cpp
@@ -702,6 +702,11 @@ llama_token common_sampler_sample(struct common_sampler * gsmpl, struct llama_co
                     // grammar_first=false CPU flow: rbudget -> grmr -> chain)
                     gsmpl->set_raw_logits(ctx, idx);
 
+                    // [TAG_CONSTRAINT_REJECT] the pending backend draw was made against the
+                    // unconstrained distribution: discard it so the resample draws a fresh
+                    // uniform and accept() does not double-advance the host RNG
+                    llama_sampler_backend_reject(chain);
+
                     llama_sampler_apply(gsmpl->rbudget, &cur_p);
 
                     if (gsmpl->grmr && grammar_should_apply(gsmpl)) {
@@ -745,6 +750,11 @@ llama_token common_sampler_sample(struct common_sampler * gsmpl, struct llama_co
                 // downloaded for grammar sequences by the server via llama_set_need_raw_logits)
                 gsmpl->set_raw_logits(ctx, idx);
 
+                // [TAG_CONSTRAINT_REJECT] the pending backend draw was made against the
+                // unconstrained distribution: discard it so the resample draws a fresh
+                // uniform and accept() does not double-advance the host RNG
+                llama_sampler_backend_reject(chain);
+
                 // [TAG_BUDGET_BACKEND] keep the budget force intact if both are active:
                 // rbudget first (mask to the forced token), then grammar, then chain —
                 // same order as the grammar_first=false CPU flow
@@ -773,6 +783,40 @@ llama_token common_sampler_sample(struct common_sampler * gsmpl, struct llama_co
         }
     }
 
+    // [TAG_CONSTRAINT_FULLVOCAB] when the backend produced no token for this position, the
+    // sampled candidates may already be filtered by the backend prefix (top-k/top-p/...):
+    // a pending grammar or forced token outside that set could never be produced and the
+    // terminal CPU stage would fail (all -inf -> NaN, or a forbidden singleton). Rebuild the
+    // candidates from the raw logits and run the entire chain on the CPU with the constraints
+    // applied first, mirroring the rejection resample above. Constrained sequences must have
+    // llama_set_need_raw_logits enabled (the server does for grammar and budget sequences).
+    {
+        const bool forcing = rbudget &&
+            common_reasoning_budget_get_state(rbudget) == REASONING_BUDGET_FORCING;
+        const bool grammar_pending = grmr && grammar_should_apply(gsmpl);
+
+        if ((forcing || grammar_pending) &&
+                (llama_get_sampled_candidates_ith(ctx, idx) != nullptr ||
+                 llama_get_sampled_logits_ith(ctx, idx) != nullptr) &&
+                llama_get_raw_logits_ith(ctx, idx) != nullptr) {
+            gsmpl->set_raw_logits(ctx, idx);
+
+            if (rbudget) {
+                llama_sampler_apply(rbudget, &cur_p);
+            }
+
+            if (grammar_pending) {
+                llama_sampler_apply(grmr, &cur_p);
+            }
+
+            llama_sampler_chain_apply_cpu(chain, &cur_p);
+
+            GGML_ASSERT(cur_p.selected != -1 && "no selected token during sampling - check your sampling configuration");
+
+            return cur_p.data[cur_p.selected].id;
+        }
+    }
+
     // apply reasoning budget first
     llama_sampler_apply(rbudget, &cur_p);
 
